.TH "ngspicetclbridge" 3tcl 0\&.5 "ngspicetclbridge" "Tcl NgspiceTclBridge package"
.SH NAME
ngspicetclbridge - Commands in namespace ngspicetclbridge
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBconfigure\fP \fI?option?\fP
.br
\fBconfigure\fP \fI?-output list|vector?\fP
.br
\fBgetCircuit\fP \fI?-logical|-physical|-deck|-expand|-runnable|-param? sim\fP
.br
\fBgetCircuitTitle\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
\fBgetPlotDate\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
\fBgetPlotName\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
\fBgetScaleInfo\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
\fBnew\fP \fI?-nospinit|-nospiceinit|-noinit? libpath ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-namespace name?\fP
.br
\fBreadVecsAsync\fP \fI?-info? ?-output list|vector? ?-namespace name? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-names dictionary|#auto? sim\fP
.br
\fBrun\fP \fI?args?\fP
.br
\fBSIM\fP \fIsubcommand \&.\&.\&.\fP
.br
\fBSIM abort\fP
.br
\fBSIM asyncvector\fP \fIname ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-name vectorName? ?-namespace name?\fP
.br
\fBSIM asyncvector\fP \fI-info name\fP
.br
\fBSIM circuit\fP \fI?-string? circuit\fP
.br
\fBSIM command\fP \fIstring\fP
.br
\fBSIM destroy\fP
.br
\fBSIM eventcounts\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
\fBSIM initvectors\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
\fBSIM inputpath\fP \fI-current\fP
.br
\fBSIM inputpath\fP \fIpath\fP
.br
\fBSIM isrunning\fP
.br
\fBSIM messages\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
\fBSIM plot\fP \fI-all\fP
.br
\fBSIM plot\fP \fI-vecs name\fP
.br
\fBSIM vectors\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
\fBSIM waitevent\fP \fIname ?-n N? ?timeout_ms?\fP
.br
.SH ::NGSPICETCLBRIDGE
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBconfigure\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Queries or changes package-wide representation defaults in this Tcl interpreter\&.
.RS 4n
\fBconfigure\fP \fI?option?\fP
.br
\fBconfigure\fP \fI?-output list|vector?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-output mode
Default output representation: list or vector; initially list\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
With no arguments, returns all settings as an option/value dictionary\&. With one option, returns its value\&.
With option/value pairs, validates all settings before applying them and returns the complete configuration\&.
Invalid options, invalid modes, or unavailable RBC support leave the configuration unchanged\&. Selecting
vector mode requires an RBC-enabled build and a loadable rbc::vector package; list queries/settings do not
load RBC\&. Defaults are independent in separate interpreters\&.
.PP
New simulator handles capture this default unless -output is supplied explicitly at creation\&.
Existing handles retain their settings\&. Per-read overrides take precedence over the handle default\&.
This public command is not namespace-exported; call it as ::ngspicetclbridge::configure\&.
Namespace selection, naming and collision policies are unaffected\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
set saved [::ngspicetclbridge::configure]
::ngspicetclbridge::configure -output vector
::ngspicetclbridge::configure -output
::ngspicetclbridge::configure {*}$saved
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
selected option value for a single-option query; otherwise all settings as a dictionary\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBgetCircuit\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets list with currently loaded circuit (its listing) in the form specified by the switch\&.
.RS 4n
\fBgetCircuit\fP \fI?-logical|-physical|-deck|-expand|-runnable|-param? sim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-deck
Just like the physical listing, except without the line numbers it recreates the input file verbatim (except that it does not preserve case)
.TP
-expand
The circuit is printed with all subcircuits expanded\&.
.TP
-logical
The circuit is with all continuation lines collapsed into one line\&.
.TP
-param
Printing all parameters and their actual values\&.
.TP
-physical
The circuits lines are printed out as they were found in the file\&.
.TP
-runnable
Circuit netlist expanded, but without additional line numbers, ready to be sourced again and run in ngspice\&. Default version if no witch is provided\&.
.TP
sim
Simulator handler that is returned by ngspicetclbridge::new
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
list with listing lines
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBgetCircuitTitle\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets title of the current circuit (first line of circuits netlist)\&.
.RS 4n
\fBgetCircuitTitle\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
sim
Not documented\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
title
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBgetPlotDate\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets time stamp of current plot generation\&.
.RS 4n
\fBgetPlotDate\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
sim
Not documented\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
time stamp
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBgetPlotName\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets name of the current plot, i\&.e\&. Operating Point, AC Analysis, etc\&.
.RS 4n
\fBgetPlotName\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
sim
Not documented\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
name of the plot
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBgetScaleInfo\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets dictionary with information about current scale vector\&.
.RS 4n
\fBgetScaleInfo\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
sim
Not documented\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dictionary with the information
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBnew\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Load dynamic library, path should be provided in native form for target OS\&.  Every ::ngspicetclbridge::new
returns a command (e\&.g\&. ::ngspicetclbridge::s1)\&. The following subcommands operate on that instance\&.
Optionally the spinit and/or spiceinit initialization files could be forbidden for loading\&.
.RS 4n
\fBnew\fP \fI?-nospinit|-nospiceinit|-noinit? libpath ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-namespace name?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-ifexists
Error (default) or replace for initial vector destinations\&.
.TP
-namespace
Destination for live vectors and snapshots; created at handle construction if missing\&.
.TP
-noinit
Inhibit both spinit and spiceinit\&.
.TP
-nospiceinit
Inhibits spiceinit\&.
.TP
-nospinit
Inhibits spinit\&.
.TP
-output
List or vector; inherits the package configuration (initially list); controls live storage and snapshots\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Namespace:
.TP
\(bu
Relative names resolve against the handle creation caller; the fully qualified name is retained\&.
.TP
\(bu
Missing namespaces and parents are created\&. Empty names are rejected\&.
.TP
\(bu
Destroying the handle does not delete the namespace\&.
.TP
\(bu
Without this option, live vectors use the creation namespace; snapshots use their caller's namespace\&.
.TP
\(bu
Use a dedicated namespace to avoid collisions, such as the signal time and Tcl's global time command\&.
.PP
Vector output:
.TP
\(bu
Requires an RBC-enabled build and rbc::vector with literal-name support\&.
.TP
\(bu
With replace, existing same-type vectors are adopted, preserving their commands and graph clients\&.
.TP
\(bu
Unrelated commands and vectors maintained by another simulator cannot be replaced\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
set sim [::ngspicetclbridge::new /usr/local/lib/libngspice\&.so]
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
command name to work with Ngspice instance, references as SIM later
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBreadVecsAsync\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Reads all available vectors of the current plot as independent snapshots\&. Returns a dictionary with
raw vector names as keys and lists or fully qualified RBC vector names as values\&.
.RS 4n
\fBreadVecsAsync\fP \fI?-info? ?-output list|vector? ?-namespace name? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-names dictionary|#auto? sim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-ifexists
Error or replace; overrides the simulator collision policy\&.
.TP
-info
Return vector metadata instead of data; cannot be combined with output options\&.
.TP
-names
#auto for fresh vectors, or a dictionary of signal names to explicit destinations or #auto
.TP
-namespace
Destination namespace for vector snapshots; created if missing, relative to the caller\&.
.TP
-output
List or vector; overrides the simulator default\&.
.TP
sim
Simulator handler that is returned by ngspicetclbridge::new
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Output and ownership:
.TP
\(bu
Handle defaults apply unless overridden\&. Without an explicit namespace, snapshots use the caller's namespace\&.
.TP
\(bu
Complex data produces complex RBC vectors\&. Snapshots survive simulator destruction\&.
.PP
Naming:
.TP
\(bu
Naming options require vector output\&. RBC generates returned names in the selected namespace\&.
.TP
\(bu
Signals omitted from -names keep signal-derived names\&.
.TP
\(bu
#auto requests automatic naming; auto without # is an ordinary name\&.
.PP
Consistency and errors:
.TP
\(bu
Vectors are copied separately; reading a running simulation is not an atomic snapshot\&.
.TP
\(bu
If a later copy fails, previously created or replaced snapshots remain in the destination namespace\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dictionary
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBrun\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Runs simulation in background thread, waits for the completion, process event in the queue and returns
.RS 4n
\fBrun\fP \fI?args?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
sim
Simulator handler that is returned by ngspicetclbridge::new -nocleanup -if provided, results from previous run are retained\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
A
command
ensemble\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM\fP \fIsubcommand \&.\&.\&.\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The ensemble supports the following subcommands:
.RS 4n
.TP
\fIabort\fP
Sets an internal abort flag and wake any waiters (useful to force waitevent to return)\&. This does \fBnot\fP free the instance\&.
.TP
\fIasyncvector\fP
Fetches the current values of a named vector through ngspice's ngGet_Vec_Info\&. Available once the simulation has produced data; the vector may still be incomplete\&.
.TP
\fIcircuit\fP
Sends an circuit to Ngspice in form of the Tcl list, each element is the line of the netlist\&. If switch -string is provided, the input netlists could be passed as ordinary string with newline character as a separator between netlists lines\&.
.TP
\fIcommand\fP
Sends an arbitrary Ngspice command line (e\&.g\&., bg_run, circbyline \&.\&.\&., \&.save, \&.tran, \&.dc)\&. If we provide -capture switch, it returns not only the result code, but also the next message from stdout of Ngspice\&. Also, if command is send in the moment background thread is starting or stopping, it will be deferred to the time is could be safely sent, and in that case -capture message and command results code are not availaible as a return of command\&.
.TP
\fIdestroy\fP
Deletes the instance command\&. In details:
.TP
\fIeventcounts\fP
Gets or reset the cumulative event counters for this simulator instance\&.
.TP
\fIinitvectors\fP
Gets held \fBinitial vector metadata\fP (built from send_init_data) in a dict\&.
.TP
\fIinputpath\fP
Gets current path for XSPICE code models if -current switch is provided, or set current path to value provided\&.
.TP
\fIisrunning\fP
Calls asynchronously to check if background thread is running\&.
.TP
\fImessages\fP
Queues of textual messages captured from Ngspice (stdout/stderr) and bridge status lines\&.
.TP
\fIplot\fP
Gets current plot name if no arguments provided, names of all plots or all vectors names that belongs to name of the provided plot\&.
.TP
\fIvectors\fP
Gets data accumulated from send_data events through the Tcl event loop\&.
.TP
\fIwaitevent\fP
Blocks until a named event is observed n number of times (or once), the instance is aborted/destroyed, or the timeout expires (if provided)\&.
.RE
.PP
Refer to the documentation of each subcommand for details\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM abort\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Sets an internal abort flag and wake any waiters (useful to force waitevent to return)\&. This does \fBnot\fP free
the instance\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM abort\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
nothing\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM asyncvector\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Fetches the current values of a named vector through ngspice's ngGet_Vec_Info\&. Available once the simulation
has produced data; the vector may still be incomplete\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM asyncvector\fP \fIname ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-name vectorName? ?-namespace name?\fP
.br
\fBSIM asyncvector\fP \fI-info name\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-ifexists
Error or replace; overrides the handle collision policy\&.
.TP
-info
Returns a metadata dictionary: signal type, real/complex type and length\&.
.TP
-name
Destination name or #auto for a fresh RBC name (vector output only)
.TP
-namespace
Destination namespace; created with missing parents (vector output only)
.TP
-output
List or vector; overrides the handle default for this snapshot\&.
.TP
name
Ngspice vector name\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Ownership and replacement:
.TP
\(bu
Vector output creates an independent, caller-owned snapshot that survives handle destruction\&.
.TP
\(bu
With -ifexists replace, existing same-type snapshot vectors are updated in place\&. Unrelated commands and live vectors maintained by any simulator cannot be overwritten\&.
.PP
Destination namespace:
.TP
\(bu
Uses the explicit handle -namespace, or otherwise the caller's namespace\&.
.TP
\(bu
A per-call -namespace overrides this selection and resolves relative to the caller\&. It does not change handle defaults or live bindings\&. Empty names are rejected\&.
.TP
\(bu
A fully qualified -name overrides the selected namespace; its parent must already exist\&.
.TP
\(bu
#auto creates a fresh RBC vector in the selected namespace\&.
.PP
Signal-derived names and access:
.TP
\(bu
Balanced parentheses, including v(1), remain literal\&. Names unsafe for RBC or containing namespace separators are encoded as _raw_ followed by uppercase hexadecimal UTF-8 bytes\&.
.TP
\(bu
No mapped array variable is created\&. Read values through the vector command, for example: \fI$vector\fP range 0 end\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim initvectors
$sim asyncvector out
# -> {0\&.0 0\&.066666\&.\&.\&. 0\&.133333\&.\&.\&. \&.\&.\&.}

$sim asyncvector V(9)
# -> {{0\&.01 0\&.00} {0\&.02 0\&.00} \&.\&.\&.}   ;# if complex
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
real vectors as a flat list of doubles, complex vectors as a list of {re im} pairs\&. Error if vector
does not exists\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM circuit\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Sends an circuit to Ngspice in form of the Tcl list, each element is the line of the netlist\&. If switch
-string is provided, the input netlists could be passed as ordinary string with newline character as a
separator between netlists lines\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM circuit\fP \fI?-string? circuit\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-string
Allows to pass circuit as ordinary string\&.
.TP
circuit
List of string\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
set resDivCircuit {
    Resistor divider
    v1 in 0 1
    r1 in out 1e3
    r2 out 0 2e3
    \&.dc v1 0 5 0\&.1
    \&.save all
    \&.end
}
$sim circuit [split $resDivCircuit \\n]
$sim command bg_run
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Ngspice result code
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM command\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Sends an arbitrary Ngspice command line (e\&.g\&., bg_run, circbyline \&.\&.\&., \&.save, \&.tran, \&.dc)\&. If
we provide -capture switch, it returns not only the result code, but also the next message from stdout
of Ngspice\&. Also, if command is send in the moment background thread is starting or stopping, it will be
deferred to the time is could be safely sent, and in that case -capture message and command results code
are not availaible as a return of command\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM command\fP \fIstring\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
string
Command string\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim command {circbyline v1 in 0 1}
$sim command bg_run
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Ngspice result code, or dictionary with result code and the message
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM destroy\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Deletes the instance command\&. In details:
.RS 4n
\fBSIM destroy\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.TP
\(bu
Marks the context as destroying
.TP
\(bu
Wakes any waiters
.TP
\(bu
Quiesces the ngspice background thread
.TP
\(bu
Defers and performs full cleanup
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
nothing\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM eventcounts\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets or reset the cumulative event counters for this simulator instance\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM eventcounts\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-clear
Zeros all counts and returns nothing\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim eventcounts
# -> send_char N  send_stat N  controlled_exit N send_data N  send_init_data N  bg_running N
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
returns a dict with keys as events names, and counts for each event as a value
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM initvectors\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets held \fBinitial vector metadata\fP (built from send_init_data) in a dict\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM initvectors\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-clear
Empties the internal memory structure and returns \fBnothing\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim initvectors
# -> out {number 1 real 1} in {number 2 real 1} v-sweep {number 3 real 1}
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBWarning\fP: accumulation of data \fBdo not\fP continues after call bg_run, new metadata replace the old one
in the storage\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dict with initial vector metadata saved in internal structure
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM inputpath\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets current path for XSPICE code models if -current switch is provided, or set current path to value
provided\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM inputpath\fP \fI-current\fP
.br
\fBSIM inputpath\fP \fIpath\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-current
Switch to return current path\&.
.TP
path
Full path to desired location\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
current path
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM isrunning\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Calls asynchronously to check if background thread is running\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM isrunning\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
1 if thread is running, 0 otherwise\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM messages\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Queues of textual messages captured from Ngspice (stdout/stderr) and bridge status lines\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM messages\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-clear
Empties the internal queue structure and returns \fBnothing\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
join [$sim messages] \\n
# stdout ******
# stdout ** ngspice-44\&.x shared library
# \&.\&.\&.
# # status[0]: --ready--
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBWarning\fP: accumulation of messages continues even if you run new circuit or analysis until you explicitly
clear the data storage\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
list of messages
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM plot\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets current plot name if no arguments provided, names of all plots or all vectors names that belongs to
name of the provided plot\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM plot\fP \fI-all\fP
.br
\fBSIM plot\fP \fI-vecs name\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-all
Switch to return all plots names\&.
.TP
-vecs plotname
Switch with argument to get all vectors names belonging to name plot\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
current plot, or list of all plots, or list of all vectors
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM vectors\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets data accumulated from send_data events through the Tcl event loop\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM vectors\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-clear
Empties stored samples and returns \fBnothing\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Output:
.TP
\(bu
List mode: dictionary mapping signal names to lists\&. Complex samples use interleaved real/imaginary doubles\&.
.TP
\(bu
Vector mode: dictionary mapping raw signal names to fully qualified live RBC vector commands\&. Real and complex signals use the corresponding vector types\&.
.PP
Updates and clearing:
.TP
\(bu
Vector identities remain stable across runs\&. Each new plot clears retained vectors, including signals absent from that plot\&.
.TP
\(bu
Updates require Tcl event processing; eventcounts/waitevent alone do not guarantee that queued vector updates have been processed\&.
.TP
\(bu
In vector mode, -clear empties vectors and discards queued samples without destroying the vectors\&. Later samples continue appending\&. Ngspice snapshot data is unaffected\&.
.PP
Ownership and renaming:
.TP
\(bu
The handle destroys vectors it created; adopted vectors remain alive\&.
.TP
\(bu
Treat live contents as read-only\&. Deleting, resizing or replacing attached vectors invalidates continued streaming\&.
.TP
\(bu
Use rbc::vector rename oldName newName to rename a live vector\&. Its identity, ownership and streaming connection are preserved across clear and subsequent runs\&.
.TP
\(bu
After renaming completes, query the bridge for the updated dictionary: signal keys remain unchanged, while destination names reflect the rename\&.
.TP
\(bu
Ordinary Tcl rename is unsupported because it leaves RBC's registry unchanged\&.
.PP
Errors:
.TP
\(bu
Asynchronous output failures are reported once through Tcl's background error handler and on subsequent vectors calls\&. Incoming samples are discarded until a new plot initializes output\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim vectors
# -> v(out) {0\&.0 0\&.1 0\&.2 \&.\&.\&.} v(in) {\&.\&.\&.} v-sweep {\&.\&.\&.}

$sim vectors -clear
# -> (no result; succeeds)
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dict with vectors values accumulated up to this point in internal structure
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM waitevent\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Blocks until a named event is observed n number of times (or once), the instance is aborted/destroyed,
or the timeout expires (if provided)\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM waitevent\fP \fIname ?-n N? ?timeout_ms?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-n N
Number of events that should happend for termination after waiting is started\&.
.TP
name
Name of the event\&.
.TP
timeout_ms
Timeout in miliseconds, optional\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
.nf
┌─────────────────┬──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Event name      │ Ngspice callback         │ When it is called                                                       │
│                 │ function name            │                                                                         │
├─────────────────┼──────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ send_char       │ SendChar                 │ Whenever Ngspice produces a line of text on stdout or stderr\&.           │
│ send_stat       │ SendStat                 │ When Ngspice’s simulation status changes (e\&.g\&., --ready--, tran 50\&.1%,  │
│                 │                          │ convergence messages)\&.                                                  │
│ controlled_exit │ ControlledExit           │ When Ngspice exits, either due to an error or after a quit command from │
│                 │                          │ Tcl/Ngspice\&.                                                            │
│ send_data       │ SendData                 │ During an analysis, whenever Ngspice sends a row of vector values (time │
│                 │                          │ step or sweep point) to the callback\&.                                   │
│ send_init_data  │ SendInitData             │ At the start of a run, when Ngspice sends metadata for all vectors in   │
│                 │                          │ the current plot (names, types, indexes, real/complex)\&.                 │
│ bg_running      │ BGThreadRunning          │ When the Ngspice background thread changes state: running=false means   │
│                 │                          │ it just started running, running=true means it has stopped\&.             │
└─────────────────┴──────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

.fi
.PP
.nf
┌──────┬─────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┬─────────────────────┐
│ Time │ Tcl Script Action       │ Ngspice Core Activity       │ Bridge Callback Fired  │ Tcl Event Name Seen │
├──────┼─────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
│ t0   │ set s [\&.\&.::new \&.\&.]      │ Library loaded              │ (none)                 │ (none)              │
│ t1   │ $s init                 │ Initialization completed    │ (none)                 │ (none)              │
│ t2   │ cirPass …               │ Parses circuit line         │ send_char("\&.\&.\&.")       │ send_char           │
│ t3   │ (more circbyline calls) │ Parses circuit line         │ send_char("\&.\&.\&.")       │ send_char           │
│ t4   │ $s command bg_run       │ Start background simulation │ bg_running(false)      │ bg_running          │
│ t5   │ (analysis setup)        │ Build vector table          │ send_init_data()       │ send_init_data      │
│ t6   │ (analysis running)      │ First data point            │ send_data(\&.\&.\&.)         │ send_data           │
│ t7   │ (analysis running)      │ More points                 │ send_data(\&.\&.\&.)         │ send_data           │
│ t8   │ (analysis running)      │ Status change               │ send_stat("\&.\&.\&.")       │ send_stat           │
│ t9   │ (analysis completed)    │ Simulation ready            │ send_stat("--ready--") │ send_stat           │
│ t10  │ (BG thread exits)       │ Background thread exits     │ bg_running(true)       │ bg_running          │
│ t11  │ $s command quit         │ ngspice quits               │ controlled_exit(\&.\&.\&.)   │ controlled_exit     │
│ t12  │ $s destroy              │ Teardown                    │ (no further calls)     │ (command removed)   │
└──────┴─────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┴─────────────────────┘

.fi
.PP
Result dictionary of the command:
.TP
\(bu
fired - 0|1, whether the event occurred during this wait
.TP
\(bu
count - cumulative total count for that event so far
.TP
\(bu
status - ok | timeout | aborted
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim waitevent send_stat 1000
# -> {fired 1 count 1 status ok}

$sim waitevent send_stat 1000
# -> {fired 0 count 1 status timeout}  ;# nothing new in the next 1s
.fi
.RE
.PP
If you want “fresh” waits, you can clear counts with eventcounts -clear\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dictionary with information about event


